<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rosa Luxemburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1871">1871</a>–<a href="/years/1919">1919</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Róża Luksemburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rosa Luxemburg was a Polish and naturalised-German Marxist theorist and revolutionary, a leading theorist of the Social <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-party-united-states">Democratic Party</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> (SPD). Born in Russian-ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> to a secular Jewish family, she co-founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/social-democracy">Social Democracy</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> and moved to Germany in 1898. In Social Reform or Revolution? (1900) she answered the reformism of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eduard-bernstein">Eduard Bernstein</a>, and in The Accumulation of Capital (1913) she tied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imperialism">imperialism</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capitalism">capitalism</a>'s need to expand. Imprisoned for most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">World War I</a> for opposing it, she co-founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spartacus">Spartacus</a> League and the Communist Party of Germany, and was killed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freikorps">Freikorps</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spartacist-uprising">Spartacist uprising</a> of 1919.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rosa-luxemburg.jpg" alt="Rosa Luxemburg" width="330" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rosa_Luxemburg_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
